15 < 1 
17 > 1 - `**Bootstrap:** bun install` — the setup the engine runs before any builder opens
18 < 1 - `- Check: bunx tsc --noEmit && bun test` — under `## Global Constraints`, run on every tested snapshot
19 < 1 - `**Dependencies:** tinybase react react-dom dev: @types/bun typescript`
16 < 2 - **testCmd:** bunx tsc --noEmit && bun test
17 < 2 - **bootstrapCmd:** bun install
18 < 2 - **Dependencies:** tinybase react react-dom dev: @types/bun typescript
19 < 1 
20 < 1 Write the first two exactly as above. Bare `tsc` requires a global TypeScript
21 < 1 install; `bunx tsc` resolves the project's own devDependency — which is what
22 < 1 keeps a fresh clone's bootstrap to a single `bun install` with nothing but Bun
23 < 1 present.
24 < 1 
25 < 1 The third row is the plan's own: a TinyApp plan names every package it needs on
26 < 1 that one header line, the specs before the single `dev:` word installed for the
27 < 1 app and the ones after it installed as development-only. A package is declared
28 < 1 there and nowhere else — no task adds one by editing `package.json`,
29 < 1 `bunfig.toml` or `bun.lock`, and a manifest on a task's Files list is edited for
30 < 1 a script or a config field, never for a dependency.
