32 < 1 ## Why it earns the restriction
33 < 1 
35 > 1 `Consumes:`/`Produces:` stop being prose a person has to eyeball. Running
34 < 2 `Consumes:`/`Produces:` stop being prose a reviewer has to eyeball. Running
35 < 1 `tsc --noEmit` over the integrated tree catches cross-task interface drift
36 < 1 deterministically, and interface drift is *the* characteristic failure of
37 < 1 parallel implementation: each task is green alone and the seam between them is
39 > 1 not. `bun test` is fast enough that a builder can afford the whole suite
38 < 2 not. `bun test` is fast enough that an implementer can afford the whole suite
39 < 1 on every iteration, so a task never trades coverage for turnaround.
