192 < 1 ## The engine boundary
193 < 1 
195 > 1 The ultrapowers engine runs whatever `**Bootstrap:**` and `Check:` lines the plan
196 < 1 names and knows nothing about Bun. This page is **authoring guidance**: it changes what a plan writes
194 < 2 The ultrapowers engine runs whatever `testCmd` it is handed and knows nothing
195 < 2 about Bun. This page is **authoring guidance**: it changes what a plan writes
196 < 1 down, never how a run executes.
197 < 1 
198 < 1 ## The baseline rule
199 < 1 
201 > 1 Any greenfield plan run on the fleet must start from a tree whose run-wide
202 < 1 `Check:` is **green at BASE**: a Check already red before any work is a red no
203 < 1 task owns (authoring-gotchas.md). So a greenfield plan driven through
204 < 1 `/ultrapowers` starts from a seeded, passing skeleton — for a TinyApp,
205 < 1 `skills/ultrawrite/stories/scaffold.ts`.
200 < 2 Any Bun fixture or greenfield plan run on the fleet must start from a tree that
201 < 2 is **green at BASE**. A tree whose tests do not exist yet cannot pass knob
202 < 2 validation, so a greenfield plan driven through `/ultrapowers` starts from a
203 < 2 seeded, passing skeleton — see the Bun eval fixture for the shape.
204 < 1 